'' A SCAN LISTS EVERY MODULE-LEVEL MACRO, however many procedure types and declarations
'' came before it. The preprocessor's block count took each 'declare const function',
'' 'declare static sub', 'declare virtual function', field or variable 'as sub( )',
'' 'type Fn as function( )' and result 'as function( )' for an opened SUB or FUNCTION, so
'' every macro after them sat at a depth nothing closed and was left out of the scan. A
'' macro inside a real SUB is scoped to it, as fbc's is, and is not listed.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-scan tests/api/src/scandepth.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: define AFTER_FORMS  @0:11:9  parent=-1
'' EXPECT-OUT: define AFTER_REAL  @0:19:9  parent=-1
'' EXPECT-NOT: INSIDE_REAL
